  "body": "Follow-up to #35, which landed pocket and slot recognition headless: `camcraft_app::recognize::pockets_of` (closed and open pockets, straight slots with open, round or square ends), `recognize::operation_for` (the Pocket or Slot that machines one), and the MCP tool `detect_pockets`. The app has no way to reach it yet.\n\n**Wanted:** a GUI entry point, e.g. a \"Detect pockets / slots\" action for the selected model (model context menu or the 2D ribbon) that:\n- lists the recognised features (kind, floor Z, depth, tightest inside corner, slot width, open sides) and highlights each floor in the viewport when hovered;\n- creates the chosen feature's operation through `CreateOperation` with the active tool, one undo step, exactly as `detect_pockets {create}` does - no logic in `ui`, only calls into `app::recognize` (layering ui -> app).\n\n**Done means:** a model with a pocket and a slot shows both in the list, and creating each adds a Pocket / Slot whose parameters page shows the recognised area and depths; Ctrl+Z removes it. Pinned by a `crates/ui/tests` event test.\n\nPart of #35.\n",
